  "prefLabel": "Per 102.10 Appointing authority",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Per 102.10 “Appointing authority” means the officer, director, board, commission, person, or designee, within an agency having the power to make appointments or assignments in the state classified service.\n\nSource. #5373, eff 4-27-92; ss by #6729, eff 4-21-98; ss by #8735, eff 10-18-06; ss by #10801, eff 5-17-15; renumbered by #13667 (formerly Per 102.07); renumbered by #14132-A; ss by #14434 (formerly Per 102.09), eff 12-1-25",
